WEBVTT

00:00:00.057 --> 00:00:03.137
All right, a lot of business happens through conversations.

00:00:03.680 --> 00:00:06.830
Calls with clients, prospective customers, partners, and people

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:08.940
helping me build different projects.

00:00:09.518 --> 00:00:11.608
What I have learned is that a good meeting

00:00:11.618 --> 00:00:13.858
doesn't automatically create good follow-through.

00:00:14.078 --> 00:00:16.468
The conversation may be valuable, but once the meeting

00:00:16.478 --> 00:00:19.387
ends, somebody still has to remember what happened, write

00:00:19.397 --> 00:00:22.307
the email, update the project, and schedule whatever should

00:00:22.317 --> 00:00:24.507
happen next. I want to show you how I

00:00:24.517 --> 00:00:26.647
use Google Meet and Gemini to make all of

00:00:26.657 --> 00:00:30.620
that easier. The meeting record gives me something tangible,

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:32.540
reliable that I can return to.

00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:34.950
It also helps me get back into the context

00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:38.510
of that specific relationship instead of depending entirely on

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:41.180
my memory because my memory is not the best.

00:00:41.270 --> 00:00:44.590
I mainly use transcripts in a few different ways.

00:00:44.970 --> 00:00:46.450
They help me maintain context.

00:00:47.270 --> 00:00:50.390
I can remember the person's priorities, needs, and history.

00:00:50.790 --> 00:00:52.810
Second, they help me follow up accurately.

00:00:53.510 --> 00:00:55.690
I can confirm what was decided during the call,

00:00:55.770 --> 00:00:58.610
what questions remain, and what each person committed to.

00:00:58.667 --> 00:01:01.860
Third, they help me track work in progress, projects,

00:01:02.780 --> 00:01:04.100
opportunities, and next actions.

00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:06.540
But a transcript is business memory.

00:01:06.660 --> 00:01:08.180
It's not necessarily finished work.

00:01:08.208 --> 00:01:10.167
This is where the process usually breaks.

00:01:10.407 --> 00:01:12.837
The meeting ends, the notes are saved, but the

00:01:12.847 --> 00:01:15.667
follow-through still depends on somebody remembering to act.

00:01:15.987 --> 00:01:19.437
Email gets delayed, the tracker becomes outdated, the next

00:01:19.447 --> 00:01:21.127
conversation never gets scheduled.

00:01:21.250 --> 00:01:23.947
So capturing the meeting isn't the entire solution.

00:01:24.067 --> 00:01:27.177
The real opportunity is using that captured information to

00:01:27.187 --> 00:01:28.467
move the work forward.

00:01:28.538 --> 00:01:31.918
